"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915096223},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I understand the schemas:\n\nFarmers Markets table:\n- state_name: state name\n- state_abbr: state abbreviation\n- farmers_markets: the count of farmers markets\n\nCensus table:\n- NAME: state name\n- POPESTIMATE2025: population estimate for 2025\n\nI need to:\n1. Sum all farmers_markets from the farmers_markets table to get the total U.S. farmers markets\n2. Get the total U.S. population from the census table (likely where NAME is \"United States\" or similar, and SUMLEV indicates it's a total)\n3. Calculate farmers_markets per 100,000 residents\n\nLet me first peek at the data to understand it better. I'll start by looking at a few rows from the farmers markets data.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_017g4ejK4nyLLCpB3vCgik4K","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.limit(5)"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":287,"cacheRead":15649,"cacheWrite":1462,"totalTokens":17412,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.001435,"cacheRead":0.0015649000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.0018275,"total":0.0048414},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":182},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915096224,"responseId":"msg_011Ce789f4vr6275vJhyJUoV","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_017g4ejK4nyLLCpB3vCgik4K","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\",\"state_abbr\",\"farmers_markets\",\"csa_programs\",\"farm_stands\",\"snap_ebt_markets\",\"snap_ebt_pct\",\"organic_vendor_markets\",\"organic_pct\",\"markets_with_website\",\"website_pct\"\n\"California\",\"CA\",647,95,223,100,15.5,114,17.6,246,38.0\n\"New York\",\"NY\",555,156,272,41,7.4,45,8.1,283,51.0\n\"Pennsylvania\",\"PA\",426,102,886,18,4.2,43,10.1,226,53.1\n\"Minnesota\",\"MN\",390,62,80,101,25.9,14,3.6,14